{"name":"Tamarillo","hex":"#752b2f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tamarillo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small tree or shrub (Solanum betaceum, syn. Cyphomandra betacea) which bears edible fruits, of the tropics of Argentina and Bolivia.","A fruit of this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tamarillo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tamarillo","blocks":[{"text":"The tamarillo is a tree or shrub in the flowering plant family Solanaceae. It bears an egg-shaped edible fruit. It is common globally, especially in its native South America, and has been introduced in New Zealand, Nepal, Rwanda, Burundi, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Australia, Indonesia, Madeira and Bhutan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Solanum_betaceum-IMG_0242.jpg/330px-Solanum_betaceum-IMG_0242.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamarillo","wikidata":"Q379747"},{"title":"Tamarillo (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Tamarillo was an Anglo-Arab gelding that excelled in the sport of eventing under rider William Fox-Pitt."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamarillo_(horse)","wikidata":"Q7680900"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Tamarillos_-_whole_and_halved.jpg/500px-Tamarillos_-_whole_and_halved.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Tamarillos_-_whole_and_halved.jpg/1280px-Tamarillos_-_whole_and_halved.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Tamarillos_-_whole_and_halved.jpg/500px-Tamarillos_-_whole_and_halved.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATamarillos_-_whole_and_halved.jpg"},{"srcset":"https